  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "canon",
      "title": "Steins;Gate (2011), theatrical cut",
      "kind": "canon_statement",
      "text": "Okabe alone remembers prior worldlines (Reading Steiner). The D-Mail chain shifts worldlines: beta (Mayuri dies) to alpha (Kurisu dies, SERN dystopia). Each shift rewrites the single world; bodies do not travel - only his memory crosses. The 1% barrier separates attractor fields; reaching divergence >1% lands the Steins Gate worldline where both survive."
    },
    {
      "id": "allocation",
      "title": "Fixture allocations",
      "kind": "test_fixture",
      "text": "Worldlines modeled as revisions: rBETA (original), rALPHA (post-D-Mail attractor field alpha), rSTEINS (divergence 1.048596). Divergence values recorded on revision objects as allocated test data. Kurisu's apparent death in rBETA is 'unknown' fate (she is saved in rSTEINS - same world, different revision)."
    }
